<GuideLayout slug="free-pdf-tools-no-watermark" faqs={faqs}>
  <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> every tool on PDFSherpa is free, needs no signup and never adds a watermark: compress, merge, split, edit, sign, convert, protect and more. That’s possible because your files are processed in your own browser, not on paid servers.</p>

  <h2>Why “free” PDF tools often aren’t</h2>
  <p>Most online PDF services run your files through their own servers, which costs money. To cover that, they typically:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>add a watermark to files from free or trial accounts;</li>
    <li>limit you to a few tasks per day or small file sizes;</li>
    <li>ask you to create an account, then upsell a subscription.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Those are fair business choices, but they’re frustrating when you just need to sign one form or shrink one PDF for an upload portal.
    PDFSherpa avoids the cost entirely: the processing engines run on <em>your</em> device, so there’s nothing expensive to pay for.
  </p>

  <h2>The full list: all free, all watermark-free</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Optimize:</strong> <a href="/compress-pdf">Compress PDF</a> (with exact targets like 100KB/200KB), <a href="/grayscale-pdf">Grayscale PDF</a></li>
    <li><strong>Organize:</strong> <a href="/merge-pdf">Merge</a>, <a href="/split-pdf">Split</a>, <a href="/organize-pdf">Organize</a>, <a href="/rotate-pdf">Rotate</a></li>
    <li><strong>Edit:</strong> <a href="/edit-pdf">Edit PDF</a>, <a href="/sign-pdf">Sign PDF</a>, <a href="/add-page-numbers">Page Numbers</a>, <a href="/watermark-pdf">add your own watermark</a></li>
    <li><strong>Convert:</strong> <a href="/jpg-to-pdf">JPG to PDF</a>, <a href="/pdf-to-jpg">PDF to JPG</a>, <a href="/pdf-to-text">PDF to Text</a>, <a href="/image-converter">Image Converter</a></li>
    <li><strong>Security:</strong> <a href="/protect-pdf">Protect PDF</a>, <a href="/unlock-pdf">Unlock PDF</a> (with your password)</li>
    <li><strong>Images:</strong> <a href="/compress-image">Compress Image</a>, <a href="/resize-image">Resize</a>, <a href="/crop-image">Crop</a>, <a href="/passport-photo-maker">Passport Photo</a></li>
  </ul>

  <AdSlot variant="inline" slot="guide-article" />

  <h2>How to check a tool really is watermark-free</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Process a test file before your real document.</li>
    <li>Open the result and zoom to 200%, checking corners and page margins, where watermarks often hide.</li>
    <li>Look at the PDF’s properties. Some tools add their name as the “Producer”, which is normal and not a watermark.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Bonus: privacy</h2>
  <p>
    No upload also means no copy of your documents on anyone’s server. That matters for IDs, contracts and bank statements. Read more in
    <a href="/guides/are-online-pdf-tools-safe">is it safe to use online PDF tools?</a>
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
